    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0176" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1887</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-13T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1918,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. Your 185, May 20, 5 p.m. You are authorized to draw on the Department up to
                    $5,000,000 additional to $1,000,000 already allotted for the same purpose. You
                    are to report progress at frequent intervals. Funds are to be expended only for
                    such supplies as can be controlled to the point of moving them in safety towards
                    Archangel or Vladivostok. Department assumes that members of <pb facs="0177"
                        n="127" xml:id="pg127"/> purchasing commission will enlist cooperation of
                    consular service and of the British and French to follow shipments and report at
                    once if their safety is imperiled or success of efforts liable to fail of
                    realization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
